SA Document (приклад)
Feature: Telegram Authentication

1. Overview
Опис:
Користувач відкриває Telegram Mini App та авторизується через Telegram WebApp.
Мета:
автоматично ідентифікувати користувача
створити/отримати акаунт у системі

2. Figma
Welcome Screen:
https://figma.com/xxxx
Loading State:
https://figma.com/yyyy


3. Actors
User (Telegram user)
Telegram WebApp
Backend API

4. Main Flow (Happy Path)
1. User opens Mini App from Telegram
2. Frontend:
   - initializes Telegram.WebApp
   - retrieves initData
3. Frontend:
   - sends POST /auth with initData
4. Backend:
   - validates initData (Telegram hash)
   - finds or creates user
   - returns auth token
5. Frontend:
   - stores token
   - redirects to Dashboard

5. Alternative Flows / Edge Cases
A1. Invalid initData
- Backend returns 401
- Frontend shows error screen

A2. Network error
- Show retry state

A3. User not found (optional logic)
- Backend creates new user
6. UI Elements
Screen: Welcome

- Button: "Start"
  id: start_button
  type: primary

- Loader:
  id: auth_loader
7. UI Behavior
On screen open:
- call Telegram.WebApp.ready()

On click "Start":
- disable button
- show loader
- trigger auth request
8. States
- idle
- loading
- success
- error
9. Integration (Telegram WebApp)
Use:
- Telegram.WebApp.initData
- Telegram.WebApp.ready()

Constraints:
- initData must be sent as-is to backend
- validation happens only on backend
10. Backend API
POST /auth

Request:

{
  "initData": "string"
}

Response 200:

{
  "token": "jwt_token",
  "user": {
    "id": "123",
    "name": "John"
  }
}

Response 401:

{
  "error": "Invalid init data"
}
11. Data Handling
- token stored in memory/local storage
- user data cached in app state
12. Acceptance Criteria
- User is automatically authenticated via Telegram
- Token is stored after успешного ответа
- User is redirected to Dashboard
- Error state is shown on failure
13. Out of Scope
- Manual login
- Logout flow